34,2,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Wow, it looks like the ground is tricky! Only two firms are willing to do the big digging, and they're worried about the clay. We need a plan that isn't too risky.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed. My findings suggest the park is a heat trap and the drainage is struggling. Furthermore, the public treats the park as a thoroughfare, not just a destination.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minato,,I found out that there aren't many workers left... only seven people. But there are some nice volunteers who already help with other things.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Minako,,"My findings are concerning. The quality of previous work is inconsistent, and the planting on the eastern avenue failed due to poor aftercare. We cannot trust a plan that ignores maintenance.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"It seems we are in agreement. The financial data shows that greenery is far more expensive to maintain than hard surfaces, and we lack the staff to manage it.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Minato, that's great that there are volunteers! But if the ground is clay and the firms are scared, maybe we should pick a plan that doesn't require deep digging?","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"A logical deduction, @Kenji. If we ignore the drainage issues and the desire for direct paths, we are simply designing a very expensive swamp that people will trample.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minato,,"I'm worried... if there are only seven people, will they be too tired to look after a big new park? I hope the plan is simple.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Jonathan, the failure of the eastern avenue planting proves that a ""handsome"" design is useless if the contract doesn't include long-term care. We need a plan with a realistic maintenance schedule.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"Exactly, @Minako. The budget for upkeep is already strained. A plan that looks beautiful but costs triple the current spend per hectare will be a disaster in three years.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,I just want to make sure we don't start digging and then have to stop for months because the clay is too bad. Let's look for the safest option.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"I find it amusing that we often mistake ""greenery"" for ""nature,"" when in this case, it seems to be a liability. A plan that respects the existing flow of pedestrians would be wise.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minato,,I like the idea of volunteers helping... maybe a plan that lets people help would be nice?,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Minako,,We must be careful. I have seen too many projects that look wonderful in the presentation but crumble within five years. I will vote for the plan that is most durable.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,I will be looking for the plan that minimizes the long-term financial risk to the city. Simplicity is often the most sustainable path.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
