60,3,1,talk,Kenji,,Plan B seems the safest! Paving a plaza is much easier than digging ponds or planting a whole forest in clay soil. It won't get stuck in the mud.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Plan B is certainly the most honest. It acknowledges the park's role as a crossing point and avoids the drainage nightmare that Plan A would likely exacerbate.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minato,,I think Plan B is good because it's a plaza... it might be easier for the seven workers to clean than a big forest or a swamp.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Minako,,"Plan A and C are too risky. Given the failure of the eastern avenue planting, a ""Woodland Walk"" would likely become a ""Dead-tree Walk."" Plan B is the most durable.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,Plan B is the only one that aligns with the financial reality. Hard surfaces are significantly cheaper to maintain per hectare than wetlands or woodlands.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Kenji,,I'm glad we all agree! I was really worried about those diggers getting stuck in the clay. Plan B is the way to go.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"It is rare that we find such harmony so quickly. It seems the ""elegant"" options have been defeated by the stubborn reality of the ground.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minato,,I'm happy everyone is getting along. I hope the people who work there will be happy with the plaza too.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Minako,,"It is not about being ""happy,"" but about being sustainable. I cannot support a plan that will look like a ruin in five years. Plan B is the only responsible choice.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,Indeed. It is better to have a functional plaza than a bankrupt garden. I am satisfied with this direction.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
